From 1a1f46ea2ff42e2107817caf46aa39e011b4e501 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:46:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the player information in one frame, with the bar on
 every page

The panel changed its height with each page (387 to 742 px with the samples):
it jumped at every press of left or right. It is one frame now, as high as
the longest page can be, every row that its values can bring in the four
languages (the Dolby Vision page: its columns from 300 px and the longest of
them 420 high, as skin_check.py measures them), and nothing moves when the
page changes; the ghosts of the columns that painted the plate under each
page go.

At its foot, on every page and in the same place, the bar: the CPU and the
GPU with their temperature, the memory, the frames dropped and skipped, and
"Output of this video" with OK before it where there is an output to
choose. Where there is none, the machine takes the whole bar. Down from any
tab goes to its button, and closes the panel where it is not shown; OK on
the overview and Dolby Vision tabs still asks for the output. The foot of
the overview and of the Dolby Vision page goes into the bar; the last 10 s
of Dolby Vision (frames, longest gap, changes of L1) are rows of its page,
under the levels.

So that the longest page is as short as it can be, and nothing is said
twice:
 - Video: the decoding (pixel format, decoder, deinterlacing) goes over the
   metadata sent, as the column of the film was the longest; the connector
   and the depth of the output go to the system page.
 - System: the CPU, the GPU, the frames dropped and skipped are in the bar;
   the page says the processing (with the rendering speed and the memory in
   MB), the connection to the TV (connector, link, format, depth, VRR, the
   mode of the output: 41894 to 41904) and the playback and the versions
   (LibreELEC Hades, the build, the graphics driver, the kernel: 41905 to
   41908).

system/hades made again.
